{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. I understand you've been feeling more tired and short of breath lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been about a week. I’ve been needing oxygen all the time now—used to be just sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And your legs were swelling too, right? You increased your water pill for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I bumped my Torsemide to 125mg. It helped a little, but I still feel puffy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. And your INR came back very high—7.1. That’s why we’re keeping you in, to watch for bleeding risks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s scary. I haven’t changed my warfarin. I take it just like my nurse tells me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. It might be the new batch from a different pharmacy. We’re holding warfarin for now until your INR comes down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need a transfusion or something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, you’re not actively bleeding. We did see a positive stool test, but you’ve only had one episode. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My PCA saw blood once in my stool. I haven’t seen it again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. We won’t do a rectal exam unless needed. Your labs show mild anemia, but stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve also been more short of breath, even moving to the commode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your oxygen requirement went up. But your chest X-ray looks clear—no signs of heart failure or infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could it be my lungs? I have that ILD from my autoimmune disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your inflammatory markers—ESR and CRP are normal. CK is down from before. No sign of a flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s making it harder to breathe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We heard some wheezing. You responded well to a breathing treatment. We think it’s reactive airway disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like asthma? I’ve never had that before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can develop, especially with other lung conditions. We’ll send you home with an albuterol inhaler to use as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my back and muscle pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on Tylenol at home, and it’s helping. We don’t see signs of polymyositis flare, so we’ll keep your current meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still thirsty. My mouth is dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2149-06-11 19:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your mucous membranes are dry. We’ll make sure you’re drinking enough. We’re also checking your electrolytes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2149-06-12 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your INR is down to 5.8 today—trending in the right direction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2149-06-12 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right? When can I restart warfarin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2149-06-12 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll wait until it’s below 3. Your home nurse will check it again soon, and you’ll restart based on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2149-06-12 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my breathing? I used the albuterol last night and it helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2149-06-12 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. That supports our plan. No wheezing this morning. Keep using it as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2149-06-12 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I follow up with my pulmonologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2149-06-12 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your PCP will coordinate that. We think this is manageable with the inhaler for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2149-06-13 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 4.7, still high but improving. No signs of bleeding. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2149-06-13 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any update on the stool test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2149-06-13 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Urine culture showed contamination, not infection. Stool hasn’t been rechecked, but no new bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2149-06-13 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a bit stronger today. Less fatigued."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2149-06-13 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your oxygen saturation is 99% on 2 liters. We’re confident you can go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2149-06-13 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my other meds? I’m on so many."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2149-06-13 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home with all your usual medications except warfarin for now. We’re keeping the albuterol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2149-06-14 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your INR is stable, and you’re doing well. We’re discharging you today with services at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2149-06-14 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll use the inhaler if I wheeze and wait for the nurse to check my INR."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2149-06-14 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Call if you have chest pain, severe shortness of breath, or any bleeding. Otherwise, follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2149-06-14 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2149-06-14 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2149-06-11 18:38:00",
    "admission_end": "2149-06-14 15:18:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a complex medical history including polymyositis, interstitial lung disease, diastolic heart failure, pulmonary hypertension, and morbid obesity was admitted for fatigue, increased oxygen requirement, and a supratherapeutic INR of 7.1. She had recently increased her Torsemide for leg swelling and reported one episode of blood in her stool. Evaluation showed no evidence of heart failure exacerbation, infection, or polymyositis flare. Her dyspnea improved with albuterol treatments, leading to a new diagnosis of reactive airway disease. The elevated INR was managed by holding warfarin, with plans to restart when INR dropped below 3. She remained stable, her symptoms improved, and she was discharged home with an albuterol inhaler and home nursing for INR monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Polymyositis",
      "Other chronic pulmonary heart diseases",
      "Postinflammatory pulmonary fibrosis",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Abnormal coagulation profile",
      "Lung involvement in other diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism"
    ]
  }
}
